 📋 Investigation Steps

 1. Preparation
- Document everything
- Use write-blockers
- Capture hashes before analysis

 2. Collection
- Disk imaging (`dd`, `FTK Imager`)
- Memory acquisition (`DumpIt`, `LiME`)
- Network logs
- System logs

 3. Analysis
- File analysis
- Registry analysis
- Memory analysis
- Timeline creation

 4. Reporting
- Summary of findings
- Timeline of events
- Chain of custody
- Recommendations

---

 🛠️ Essential Commands
 Disk Imaging (Linux)
```bash
dd if=/dev/sda of=image.dd bs=4096 conv=noerror,sync
dcfldd if=/dev/sda of=image.dd hash=md5 hashlog=hash.txt
File Analysis
file suspicious_file
strings suspicious_file | less
binwalk suspicious_file
xxd suspicious_file | head

Memory Analysis (Volatility)
volatility -f memory.dmp imageinfo
volatility -f memory.dmp --profile=Win10x64 pslist
volatility -f memory.dmp --profile=Win10x64 netscan

Timeline Creation
log2timeline --hasher md5 timeline.plaso /mnt/evidence/
psort -o l2tcsv timeline.plaso > timeline.csv

